{
  "scenario_id": "2020-03",
  "events": [
    {
      "month": "2020-12",
      "title": "WHO lists a COVID-19 vaccine for emergency use",
      "description": "Its first such listing supports wider access to the Pfizer-BioNTech vaccine.",
      "source_ids": ["vaccine"]
    },
    {
      "month": "2022-03",
      "title": "The Fed starts raising interest rates",
      "description": "It raises its target for short-term rates as inflation remains high.",
      "source_ids": ["rates-2022"]
    },
    {
      "month": "2022-07",
      "title": "Webb reveals new views of space",
      "description": "NASA releases a full set of images from the powerful space telescope.",
      "source_ids": ["webb"]
    }
  ],
  "what_happened_next": {
    "text": "Netflix and the US share basket more than doubled over five years. Amazon nearly doubled, but Disney finished only slightly higher. The bond estimate fell a little. This starting date came after a sharp market fall, so it gives a different picture from buying before the outbreak.\n\nThe pandemic was already known when you invested. Later that year, WHO listed its first COVID-19 vaccine for emergency use. In 2022, the Fed began raising interest rates, and Webb released a full set of scientific images. The situation continued to change long after the urgent first headlines.\n\nDisney’s small final gain is useful beside the much larger gains elsewhere. Getting back above the starting amount is different from growing quickly. Bonds also show that a government-loan investment can lose market value. You could not know these exact paths in March 2020. A plan made then had to allow for several futures, including a slower recovery or a different set of winning companies.",
    "source_ids": [
      "french-us",
      "french-international",
      "fred-gs5",
      "yahoo-dis",
      "yahoo-amzn",
      "yahoo-nflx",
      "vaccine",
      "rates-2022",
      "webb"
    ]
  },
  "reflection": {
    "what_people_were_focused_on": "The pandemic had closed venues and changed daily life. Companies hired workers, adjusted services and tried to cope with sudden demand changes.",
    "what_actually_mattered": "The starting price mattered as well as the company. Gains measured from this month do not erase losses suffered by someone who bought earlier.",
    "what_faded_away": "A hiring plan or busy streaming service did not translate into a guaranteed stock return. Business activity and share prices are connected, but not identical.",
    "what_nobody_knew": "The length of the disruption, the recovery and later interest rates were uncertain. The final chart leaves out how hard it felt to make choices then.",
